Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Fix USASpending NAICS/PSC mapping; add missing-field
 guards

Validated against the live USASpending spending_by_award API:
- NAICS and PSC come back as {"code","description"} objects, not strings.
  Flatten to the bare code via code_of() so leads match the cockpit schema
  (previously a dict was written into naics/psc, breaking import).
- Add warn_missing() guards on the first record of each feed so a renamed
  or dropped API field is logged loudly instead of silently dropped, per
  the project guide. SAM params/fields confirmed against the live docs;
  final SAM live check runs in the scheduled Action where the key lives.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017uh9cMntZaBTp82X6EN2pY
---
 ignitec_bd_sourcing.py | 33 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ignitec_bd_sourcing.py b/ignitec_bd_sourcing.py
index 382bf66..6944726 100644
--- a/ignitec_bd_sourcing.py
+++ b/ignitec_bd_sourcing.py
@@ -101,6 +101,29 @@ def is_warm(name):
     return any(p in n for p in WARM_PARTNERS)
 
 
+def code_of(v):
+    """USASpending returns NAICS/PSC as {"code": ..., "description": ...} objects.
+    The cockpit schema wants the bare code string. Flatten, tolerating older
+    string-shaped responses."""
+    if isinstance(v, dict):
+        return v.get("code") or ""
+    return v or ""
+
+
+# Expected result keys per feed; a live response missing one is logged loudly
+# rather than silently dropped (see project guide: "do not silently drop fields").
+USA_EXPECTED = {"Award ID", "Recipient Name", "Awarding Agency", "Award Amount",
+                "Start Date", "End Date", "NAICS", "PSC"}
+SAM_EXPECTED = {"noticeId", "title", "fullParentPathName", "naicsCode", "responseDeadLine"}
+
+
+def warn_missing(sample, expected, feed):
+    missing = [k for k in expected if k not in sample]
+    if missing:
+        print(f"  ! {feed}: response missing expected field(s): {sorted(missing)}. "
+              f"Got keys: {sorted(sample.keys())}")
+
+
